# ── Giants and supergiants ──

@star red-giant
name: Red giant
makeup: hydrogen 90.5%, helium 9.4%, oxygen 0.045%, nitrogen 0.02%, carbon 0.012%, neon 0.008%, magnesium 0.004%, silicon 0.003%, iron 0.003%, sulfur 0.0013%
makeup-note: its surface stirred up from its depths: nitrogen up, carbon down (the first dredge-up)
surface-kind: giant
real: yes
color: red-orange
stage: late life of a star of about one solar mass
tags: swollen, cool surface
radius-sol: 10..100
temp-k: 3300..5000
share-of-stars: uncommon

@star red-supergiant
name: Red supergiant
makeup: hydrogen 89%, helium 10.9%, oxygen 0.045%, nitrogen 0.03%, carbon 0.01%, neon 0.008%, magnesium 0.004%, silicon 0.003%, iron 0.003%, sulfur 0.0013%
makeup-note: deep mixing: helium and nitrogen up, carbon down
surface-kind: giant
real: yes
color: red
stage: late life of a heavy star
example: Betelgeuse
death: supernova
tags: huge, cool surface
radius-sol: 200..1500
temp-k: 3400..4100
share-of-stars: rarest

@star blue-supergiant
name: Blue supergiant
makeup: hydrogen 90%, helium 9.9%, oxygen 0.045%, nitrogen 0.02%, carbon 0.015%, neon 0.008%, magnesium 0.004%, silicon 0.003%, iron 0.003%
makeup-note: nitrogen up and carbon down at its surface, from its burning core
surface-kind: giant
real: yes
color: blue
example: Rigel
death: supernova
tags: huge, very bright
radius-sol: 20..100
temp-k: 10000..50000
share-of-stars: rarest

@star wolf-rayet
name: Wolf-Rayet star
makeup: helium 86%, hydrogen 2%, nitrogen 8%, carbon 2.5%, oxygen 1%, neon 0.2%, iron 0.03%, silicon 0.03%, magnesium 0.03%
makeup-note: its hydrogen blown away in its wind: a bare core of helium, rich in nitrogen (the WN kind)
surface-kind: normal
real: yes
color: blue
stage: heavy star blowing off its outer layers
tags: very hot, strong winds
radius-sol: 1..20
temp-k: 30000..200000
share-of-stars: rarest

