makeup: hydrogen 91%, helium 8.8%, oxygen 0.045%, carbon 0.025%, neon 0.008%, nitrogen 0.006%, magnesium 0.004%, silicon 0.003%, iron 0.003%
makeup-note: cool enough for dust clouds of iron and silicates in its air
surface-kind: brown-dwarf
real: yes
says: the warmest brown dwarfs, with metal-hydride clouds
radius-sol: 0.08..0.12
temp-k: 1300..2200
share-of-stars: uncommon

@star t-dwarf
name: T-type brown dwarf
makeup: hydrogen 91%, helium 8.8%, oxygen 0.045%, carbon 0.025%, neon 0.008%, nitrogen 0.006%, magnesium 0.004%, silicon 0.003%, iron 0.003%
makeup-note: cool enough for methane and water in its air
surface-kind: brown-dwarf
real: yes
says: cooler brown dwarfs with methane in their air
radius-sol: 0.08..0.12
